G Robert Mann <grmann@ksu.edu> writes:

[Wish in Minetown after Sokoban]
> I'm mostly trying to decide between dragon scale mail or a bag
> of holding.  If I go for dragon scale mail what kind should I get?

That's an eternal debate.  Some prefer to get a free amulet 
slot, in which case silver is preferred, some like it to have 
a free robe slot, which favors grey.  Personally, I would go 
for silver since amulets seem more appealing to me.  

> I've already got reflection (amulet in Sokoban) and magic resistance
> (starting cloak).  In favor of the bag of holding, I've been
> struggling to stay unburdened for quite a while, but Sokoban may have
> helped with that.

Not having a bag of holding is a nuisance, but if you can 
you should try to live with this until you reach the castle.  
I would rather recommend a blessed magic marker for gaining 
armor class.  

> Also, while I'm asking stuff, I've got a large cat that's up to level
> 9, should I consider polymorphing him at some point, and if so what
> should I hope to get?

The usual way to polymorph a pet is using a magic whistle 
repeatedly while standing near a poly trap.  You can get 
much better pets than a cat, but be cautious about leaving 
your pet master mind flayer alone for too long.  Personally, 
I prefer fast or teleporting pets; the other ones cost time 
and nerve to collect before leaving a level.  Good pets:  

Devils          (for style)
Leprechauns     (for buying protection)
Foocubi         (for the obvious)
Mind flayers    (kill almost anything)
* Lich          (similar, plus self-healing)
Archon          (would be cool, but never had one so far; 
                maybe you don't get them by polying)
Ki-Rin          (for riding)
Dragons         (for riding; speed them)

